MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The smart plug gives my recent Echo devices a useful new job: controlling a lamp by voice. That makes it a stronger next purchase than another speaker.",
    "The memory cards and HDMI cable fit my history of removable storage, card readers, and TV equipment, although I would buy them only when I have a specific storage or connection need."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The streaming sticks and older Echo Dot repeat functions covered by my recent Fire TV Stick 4K Max and fourth-generation Echo Dot, so their familiarity does not give me a reason to buy them.",
    "The older Fire tablet has no clear role alongside my recent Echo Show, and the wired earbuds do not address a listening need I currently have."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My purchases of Alexa devices seem to have been taken as interest in more Alexa devices, even when they would duplicate what I already use.",
    "My history of buying electronics accessories seems to have been treated as a current need for cards and cables, when those purchases depend on a particular task."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent device purchases matter because they show which needs I have already covered; older devices serving the same purpose offer little benefit right now.",
    "I respond to accessories that help me do something new with equipment I already have, as the smart plug would, while extra storage or a long cable can wait until a concrete need arises."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in home electronics but miss the difference between extending my setup and duplicating functions I recently added."
}
